<mxCell id="t3" value="FK* on owner_id / entered_by / awarded_by reference the platform&#39;s users table, which lives outside the &quot;PERF&quot; schema — informational, not drawn as an edge here. budget_category_accounts.accounting_account_id and company_id are deliberately unenforced references to &quot;ACCOUNTING&quot;.accounts.id/companies.id (Accounting is an optional install; see §3B/§5) — no edge drawn since the target table isn&#39;t part of this schema. subject_type/subject_id columns (targets, kpi_values, budget_hdrs, okr_objectives, scorecard_hdrs, achievements) are polymorphic tags, not real foreign keys — deliberately, per §5&#39;s &quot;no dedicated hierarchy table&quot; decision. Dashed edges = optional/conditional reference (nullable, depends on metric_type or is otherwise not always populated)." style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5563;align=left;fontStyle=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1596" width="1400" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
